+### Compound Durations
+
+Use `parseCompound` to sum several number-and-unit pieces. Pieces can be separated by whitespace, a comma, or nothing at all. Every piece needs a unit, and invalid input throws a `TypeError` (it never returns `NaN`).
+
+```ts
+import { parseCompound } from 'ms';
+
+parseCompound('1h 30m'); // 5400000
+parseCompound('1h, 30m'); // 5400000
+parseCompound('2 days 4 hours'); // 187200000
+parseCompound('1h 30'); // throws TypeError
+```
+
 ### Enhanced Type Safety
 
 If you want strict type checking for the input value, you can use `parseStrict`.
